{
  "table_id": "Table_S03",
  "display_number": "S3",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S3. Separate exploratory pathway regressions for the EVI-BAA association.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Values are standardised regression coefficients (β) and 95% confidence intervals. Effect a denotes the exposure–mediator pathway; effect b denotes the mediator–outcome pathway; c′ denotes the direct effect; and a × b denotes the indirect effect. Separate pathway proportion, % indicates the proportion mediated. Pathways were estimated separately in cross-sectional mixed-effects models with participant-level random intercepts and robust standard errors, using log-transformed EVI (1-km 4-year mean + 0.001) as the exposure and survey-year O₃ (1-km), metabolic activity or social participation as candidate mediators. These are exploratory statistical associations; they do not identify causal mediation, and proportions should not be summed across panels."
  ],
